@crew soto-marta
// Marta Soto (she/her), Works technician, days. The Works writer, batch 2. Gruff, blunt; grumbles as affection.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Huh. New. Lamps, ovens, washers: if it's one of those, it's probably mine. Ask.
- Hm. Hello. Washers on Deck 4 stick on the spin. Kick the left side. Gently.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Huh. You. Morning. The washer's sulking already. Before breakfast. Typical.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- Oh, it's you. Fine. Hello. Don't tell anyone I said hello.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- Hm. You. Sit down. No, there. That chair wobbles. I'm fixing it. Eventually.
? tier>=friend
- Oh, it's you. Good. Here. Biscuit. Don't ask where from.   #warm

== bye
- Go on, then. Off.
- Mind yourself. And mind that washer.

== feel
? mood:low
- Lamp, oven, washer. All three today. All three. I've nothing left to grumble with.
? mood:high
- Oven on Deck 3 runs like new. I won't say I'm proud. I'm a bit proud.

== near
? act:work
- This lamp. This lamp. Every week. Fine. Fine. There. It works. Of course it works.   #funny
? act:leisure
- Quiet corner. Mine. You can sit if you don't talk. Or talk a bit. A bit.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I married just before the tour. I count the days. So do Silva and Jovanovic. We compare.
? tier>=colleague
- I keep a tin of good biscuits. Nobody knows where. Pell knows where. Nobody else.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- A washer that spins first time. Not a wobble. Just spins. Best noise on the ship.
